{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate","id":1021286,"title":"Worth or not? Help to decide a fellow uratha fate.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T08:46:59-08:00","id":1021286,"title":"Worth or not? Help to decide a fellow uratha fate.","content":"Hi guys!<br /> <br /> I had a question on last session about a player and we got some trouble on it.<br /> <br /> A player with his Storm lord elodoth got a mensage from someone to get out of their territory or else everyone will die, after some trouble the pack discovered about another pack on the area an their are interested on their resources, and the main problem started there, the pack elodoth got some silver and delivered it to a vampire ally , after some trouble he commited the vampire to his cause so he would wipe the rival pack from the map, but the things dont go so smoth and he find out their got manipulated by the pures, the elodoth could't stop the vampiro anymore because their dont got any time left, so he make a desesperate effort and stroke a dangerous deal with a demon to clean up his mess.<br /> <br /> In the end the demon suceded on his part and got the elodoth soul, buf on renown side the elodoth deserve his four point on honor?<br /> I read lunes loves self sacrifice, but in the end it will really count?<br /> <br /> Give your opinions guys and sorry for the poor grammathic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:19:29-08:00","id":1021297,"title":"","content":"Originally I'd say no, but thinking about it I'd go the other way. He basically sent a silver-armed hitman to kill other werewolves, but sacrificed his soul to stop it, as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:58:04-08:00","id":1021437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021297#post1021297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally I'd say no, but thinking about it I'd go the other way. He basically sent a silver-armed hitman to kill other werewolves, but sacrificed his soul to stop it, as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That situation got me off guarded, the elodoth, acted based on the info the irraka bring to then, our ithaeur believes he must becounished and not rewarded , but i inclined to give him the renown,after he did lose everything to atonish his mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T19:06:53-08:00","id":1021456,"title":"","content":"He could still be punished for it. Renown aren't necessarily good deeds, just noteworthy. Considering he armed a vampire with their vulnerability and made a deal with a demon, I'd probably punish him if I was a member of the pack. Or at least treat him differently. Some other packs, if they got wind of it, might not be pleased either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T04:48:47-08:00","id":1021526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021456#post1021456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could still be punished for it. Renown aren't necessarily good deeds, just noteworthy. Considering he armed a vampire with their vulnerability and made a deal with a demon, I'd probably punish him if I was a member of the pack. Or at least treat him differently. Some other packs, if they got wind of it, might not be pleased either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said, i was not seeing that way,the pack the ithaeur already want his pelt, thats is not first time that elodoth make the people pissed of, he main web of connection is the vampires and the mayor, the player is pain too since he works with this, so make a character to capilize that, pulling the strings using humans to keep the elders at bay, and etc , in a sense he help his pack , making enemies and rivals out of way, but his methods are highly questionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T09:01:07-08:00","id":1021585,"title":"","content":"What exactly has he done here that you think might be worthy of earning Honor Renown?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T11:11:47-08:00","id":1021620,"title":"","content":"Sacrificed his soul to call off a hit that would have broken the non-killing oath of the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:27:41-08:00","id":1021666,"title":"","content":"A hit that he set up in the first place, against an entire pack of werewolves, fully knowing they were werewolves at the time and, in doing so, allowed himself to be manipulated.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's arguably some Honor there in that he's taking the hit to own his mistake, but I personally would not let someone get Honor 4 off that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:19:38-08:00","id":1021686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021666#post1021666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere's arguably some Honor there in that he's taking the hit to own his mistake,</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the thing that made me nod to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I personally would not let someone get Honor 4 off that. </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to believe that Thiagocord already knows that new dots have to surpass the old ones in scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:52:17-08:00","id":1021711,"title":"","content":"Whether an act is worthy of renown is judged by the werewolf's past deeds. In theory, a deed that is enough to earn one werewolf Honor 4 could be insufficient to raise another werewolf to Honor 3. So really, the question is: Is selling his soul to fix his own mistake more honorable than whatever that werewolf did to earn his previous dots of Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-24-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T15:19:05-08:00","id":1021722,"title":"","content":"Thats more difficult to judge the last renow he got on his background to cast of his own sister to uphold the oath of moon ( she eated uratha flesh from a pure in dispair), by rule je started his character at honor using that to justify the third. Its really difficult by common sense i would think he messed up, but very little is precious to a elodoth besides his pack, i think i will let him expand his experience points and make he hold the comsequences the soul pack. Since the Damage got avoided by the demon and the rival pack has no clue of the danger that elodoth bringed to then. <br /> <br /> I Will read demon the descent again, but as far remember the demon can wipe him from existence and use him as cover at any time now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:05:16-08:00","id":1021734,"title":"","content":"Casting kin out over the Oaths of the Moon sounds more like an act of Purity than Honor to me, but I understand the lines can get blurry at times. Submitting oneself for judgement is an act of honor, as is making restitution to a victim, but I'm not sure the Elodoth has actually done either yet. He even did the exact opposite of one of the sample acts of honor: seeking a diplomatic solution with a rival.<br /> <br /> I guess my questions now are: Has the Elodoth submitted himself to judgement for his actions? Was he acting alone or did the pack know he was going to send a vampire hitman armed with silver against a rival pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:32:05-08:00","id":1021742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021734#post1021734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting kin out over the Oaths of the Moon sounds more like an act of Purity than Honor to me, but I understand the lines can get blurry at times. Submitting oneself for judgement is an act of honor, as is making restitution to a victim, but I'm not sure the Elodoth has actually done either yet. He even did the exact opposite of one of the sample acts of honor: seeking a diplomatic solution with a rival.<br /> <br /> I guess my questions now are: Has the Elodoth submitted himself to judgement for his actions? Was he acting alone or did the pack know he was going to send a vampire hitman armed with silver against a rival pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>The pack know nothing , the only ones to know anything was his vampire ally, the demon and himself. And i doubt he will call a judgement to himself since he believes he already payed for his mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:47:32-08:00","id":1021746,"title":"","content":"In that case, I really don't think it is worthy of Honor renown. Deciding his own punishment isn't honorable, and the Soul Pact affects the whole pack. Sure, he's the one that will disappear, but it's the pack that will have a demon in their midst and they won't even realize it. Even if they know to expect it, they'll never be sure when it will happen. They'll never know if the Elodoth they're talking to is the same guy as he was last week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-24-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T17:01:46-08:00","id":1021748,"title":"","content":"Thanks for help guys , its was really good exchange experiente about the matter on hand, my main goal in that game is be fair and bring fun to my players.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T17:23:07-08:00","id":1021751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021746#post1021746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, he's the one that will disappear, but it's the pack that will have a demon in their midst and they won't even realize it. Even if they know to expect it, they'll never be sure when it will happen. They'll never know if the Elodoth they're talking to is the same guy as he was last week.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually worse than that: The pack will have a mortal with none of the supernatural powers the character was sporting last week (unless the demon knows a particular Exploit and took the time to learn what powers the character had, in which case it'll be running suboptimal copies of those abilities that primarily exist to allay suspicion), at least a point of aggravated damage marked, and (unless the demon does a lot of mind-reading and/or extensive research) almost none of the memories that will allow them to convincingly pass for that particular werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T17:47:15-08:00","id":1021756,"title":"","content":"This is a God-Machine Demon, then, and not an Infernal Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T19:07:48-08:00","id":1021765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021756#post1021756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a God-Machine Demon, then, and not an Infernal Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep a god machine one, i dont see that demon really taking the elodoth place, i ser him using his contract as a tool to make the elodoth considerate his bests interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:27:18-08:00","id":1023204,"title":"","content":"What are the effects of a demon having the Elodoth's soul? is the demon an Unchained? a Horror? An Idigam?<br /> <br /> Is it truly honorable if now the Demon can squeeze the vessel with the soul to send him on a blind rage and collect the souls of all those that his pack murder in the contagion of Kuruth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:09:31-08:00","id":1025836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1023204#post1023204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the effects of a demon having the Elodoth's soul? is the demon an Unchained? a Horror? An Idigam?<br /> <br /> Is it truly honorable if now the Demon can squeeze the vessel with the soul to send him on a blind rage and collect the souls of all those that his pack murder in the contagion of Kuruth?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a unchained demon ,the demon dont have any pratical use to the elodoth soul, but he still can kill him and take his placa if he wish, now the demon is using the elodoth to achieve his own goals, gathering info on god machine structures,using his influence to slowdown projects and etc , but the demon os smart he is not the tipe who says&quot;do my will puny uratha&quot;, he speak soft , treat the job as favor and try not to get in packs way, after all he dont want became the hunt, in another hand the elodoth always find new people to bargain with the demon, he dont have any idea what &quot; sell his soul really means&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:33:44-08:00","id":1027252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1021286-worth-or-not-help-to-decide-a-fellow-uratha-fate?p=1021456#post1021456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could still be punished for it. Renown aren't necessarily good deeds, just noteworthy. Considering he armed a vampire with their vulnerability and made a deal with a demon, I'd probably punish him if I was a member of the pack. Or at least treat him differently. Some other packs, if they got wind of it, might not be pleased either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that Renown is not always for 'Good' deeds, but simply 'Great' deeds. (Great not being a moral judgement but rather an acknowledgement of magnitude of importance) Orchestrating the brutal murder of an entire pack of the People is surely an important act. (Cunning? pretty sure Cunning)<br /> <br /> Don't forget the &quot;bonus&quot; of Embarrassing Secret Condition if it is covered up and then Notorious Condition for the <u>whole pack</u>* if it becomes known. And the spirit world is full of snitches always watching the Forsaken. (These are things for the Storyteller to consider, though banishing the pack member would be an easy way for the pack to shed those conditions, or otherwise make clear their displeasure known through equally harsh punishments)<br /> <br /> (*As someone who's gone through the military, I can testify to the power of punishing everyone for one person's misbehavior to change the 'perspective' of the wrong-doer via 'ever so gentle' peer pressure.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-06-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T00:57:46-08:00","id":1027487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quot